{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "MosaicAerosolPhaseState",
    "description": "MOSAIC's phase state of ONE size bin: SUBROUTINE aerosol_phase_state of chem/module_mosaic_therm.F (WRF v4.8.0), with the branch decisions of SUBROUTINE mesa, do_full_deliquescence / adjust_liquid_aerosol / adjust_solid_aerosol, calculate_kelvin, drh_mutual and aerosol_water_up. ASTEM calls it for every bin at the start of each of its sub-steps, after conform_electrolytes has rebuilt the bin's total electrolytes; it decides whether the bin is solid, liquid or mixed, how much water it holds, and the Kelvin factors that raise the equilibrium vapour pressures of HNO3, HCl, NH3 over a small droplet.\n\nINPUTS a consumer supplies: rh_pc, t_k, the bin's number concentration, the total species and the total electrolytes (as conform_electrolytes left them), and water_a_hyst -- the water the bin carried on the upper hysteresis leg at the end of the previous MOSAIC step (0 on the lower leg).\n\nDRY MASS AND VOLUME. sum_a A_a mw_a (and A_a mw_a / rho_a), plus the charge-balance H+ aer_H = (2 SO4 + NO3 + Cl + MSA + 2 CO3) - (2 Ca + Na + NH4), which the Fortran adds as nmol straight into the ng and ncc sums (an implied 1 g/mol and 1 g/cm3, written as such in mosaic_phase_parameters.esm), times 1e-15.\n\nTHE BRANCH (SUBROUTINE mesa, template mesa_path), tried in this order at the current water activity x: (1) x < crh = 0.35 and X_T > 1 or X_T < 0 and neither Ca(NO3)2 nor CaCl2 above ptol_mol_astem = 0.01 mol percent: effloresced, ALL SOLID. (2) water_a_hyst > 0.5 water_a_up, where water_a_up is the ZSR water of the totals at a fixed a_w = 0.6 without the kappa term (mhyst_method = uporlo_waterhyst): the upper hysteresis leg, FULLY LIQUID, water = ZSR water of the TOTAL electrolytes at x. (6) 0 < X_T < 1, the excess-sulfate domain: handed to mesa_ptc. (4) no salt above ptol_mol_astem: ALL SOLID -- which includes a pure H2SO4 or a purely carbonaceous bin on the lower leg. (5) x*100 below the mutual deliquescence RH of the salts present (jsulf_poor/jsulf_rich of the salt code, drh_mutual's cubic in T plus 1, or 10% for Ca(NO3)2/CaCl2 mixtures): ALL SOLID. (6) otherwise mesa_ptc. MESA_PTC, the pseudo-transient solid-liquid equilibrium solver (mixed phases), IS NOT TRANSCRIBED HERE: where the branch is 6, only `path` (and the inputs-only water_up and mass_dry) mean anything. The Fortran's step-2 'negative water' exit cannot occur with non-negative amounts and is omitted.\n\nTHE KELVIN ITERATION. On the liquid branch the wet volume V = vol_dry + 1e-3 W(x), the volume-mean diameter Dp = (6 V/(N pi))^(1/3), the solution tension sigma = sigma_water + 49 (1 - x), and K = 1 + t(1 + t/2 (1 + t/3)) with t = 72 sigma/(R T Dp) (R = 8.3144e7) give a new water activity x' = rh_pc 0.01/K. The loop repeats while |x' - x|/x exceeds 1e-2 (1e-6 above 99% RH), at most ten updates. It is written as a causal recurrence over the iteration axis `it` (esm 4.3.1.1): aw_it[1] = rh_pc 0.01, aw_it[i] = kelvin_update(aw_it[i-1]), where kelvin_update returns x' if the bin is liquid at x and the change exceeds the tolerance, and x otherwise -- so the sequence holds once the Fortran's loop has exited. The three CLAUDE.md tests all fail, which is why it is a recurrence: (a) it does not unroll into a reduction over original values, because each pass reads the previous pass's ANSWER through W(x) and K(x); (b) it is not an ODE integrator but a fixed-point iteration, and transcribing the converged fixed point instead would not reproduce the Fortran, whose 1e-2 tolerance routinely stops one pass early (a 0.6% Kelvin correction is never applied); (c) it is a single variable, so there is no cycle to break. The only state carried is the scalar x; W(x) is re-evaluated inside the recurrence by the zsr_water template (mosaic_thermo_templates.esm), the same expression aerosol_water_zsr.esm uses. niter counts the passes. Because the branch is re-decided on every pass, a bin just above crh can go liquid on the first pass and effloresce on the second once K has lowered x below 0.35; the Fortran then exits with ah2o_a at the lowered value and kelvin from the previous pass, which `kelvin` reproduces.\n\nOUTPUTS. ah2o_a, niter, path, state (jaerosolstate; 0 where mesa_ptc decides), jhyst (jhyst_leg), water, mass/vol wet, dpmv, sigma_soln, kelvin, kel(gas) for H2SO4, HNO3, HCl, NH3, MSA (t = 4 sigma vbar/(R T Dp), 1 when solid), and the solid/liquid partition of species and electrolytes (liquid: all but CaSO4 and CaCO3 dissolve, Ca++ in the liquid is the Ca(NO3)2 + CaCl2; solid: everything stays solid). dpmv, sigma_soln, mass_wet and vol_wet are meaningful on the liquid branch only: on a solid exit the Fortran leaves whatever the previous pass, or the previous call, put there.\n\nFORTRAN_BUGS B28: sigma_water = 0.2358 tau^1.256 (1 - 0.625 tau) is the IAPWS surface tension of water in N/m (about 0.072), and calculate_kelvin adds it to 49 (1 - a_w), a term in dyn/cm; pure water's 72 dyn/cm enters as 0.072. The solution tension, and so every Kelvin factor, is too small: at 290 K and a_w = 0.6 it is 19.7 instead of 93.3 dyn/cm (every Kelvin term 4.7 times too small), and toward a_w = 1 it falls to 0.073 instead of 73 (a thousandfold). Reproduced as written; fixing it fails 65 assertions.\n\nPRECISION. Double-precision arithmetic with the default-real literals at their binary32 values (mosaic_phase_parameters.esm): 0.35, 0.01, 0.6, 1e-15, 1e-3, 3.1415926, 1./3. (formed in REAL), 647.15, 0.2358, 1.256, 1e-2, 1e-6. rh_pc itself is 100*relhumclm formed in default REAL.\n\nTESTS AND COVERAGE. 14 hand-specified bins run through WRF's own compiled aerosol_phase_state (kernels/mosaic_therm_driver mode 2; chem170_scm/therm64/make_cases.py) reach every branch: liquid at 0.30 (Ca blocks efflorescence), 0.60, 0.90 and 0.995 (the 1e-6 tolerance), with 1 to 3 Kelvin passes; efflorescence on the first pass and on the second; no-salt solids (H2SO4, carbon); below the mutual DRH (ammonium sulfate at 0.60, NaCl + NH4NO3 at 0.50); and three mesa_ptc hand-offs. Mutation-checked: fixing B28 fails 65, a single Kelvin pass (NIT = 1) 51, two passes 13, crh = 0.30 14, the 1e-2 tolerance above 99% 13, the double-precision pi 9 and 1/3 44, dropping aer_H from the dry mass 14.",
    "authors": [
      "EqWeFiC"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Zaveri, R.A., Easter, R.C., Fast, J.D., Peters, L.K. (2008). Model for Simulating Aerosol Interactions and Chemistry (MOSAIC). J. Geophys. Res. 113, D13204."
      },
      {
        "citation": "WRF v4.8.0 chem/module_mosaic_therm.F"
      }
    ]
  },
  "metaparameters": {
    "NEL": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 22,
      "description": "Number of MOSAIC electrolytes carried (nelectrolyte is 23; the 23rd, joc, is never assigned and stays zero)."
    },
    "NZSR": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 19,
      "description": "Electrolytes that hold water, the first nsalt + 4."
    },
    "NSALT": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 15,
      "description": "Soluble salts nsalt, the electrolytes MESA's salt-combination code counts."
    },
    "NAER": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 112,
      "description": "MOSAIC aerosol species per bin (naer, chem_opt = 170 build)."
    },
    "NIT": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 11,
      "description": "Passes of the Kelvin loop: the first, plus at most ten updates (iter_kelvin <= 10)."
    }
  },
  "index_sets": {
    "el": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": "NEL"
    },
    "aer": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": "NAER"
    },
    "pc": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 6
    },
    "it": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": "NIT"
    },
    "gas": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 5
    }
  },
  "models": {
    "MosaicAerosolPhaseState": {
      "expression_template_imports": [
        {
          "ref": "./mosaic_thermo_templates.esm"
        }
      ],
      "subsystems": {
        "tp": {
          "ref": "./mosaic_thermo_parameters.esm"
        },
        "pp": {
          "ref": "./mosaic_phase_parameters.esm"
        }
      },
      "expression_templates": {
        "mesa_path": {
          "params": [
            "x"
          ],
          "description": "Which branch of SUBROUTINE mesa decides the bin at water activity x: 1 below the crystallization point (x < crh and crh_ok), all solid; 2 the upper hysteresis leg, fully deliquesced (liquid); 6 the excess-sulfate domain 0 < X_T < 1, or a salt mixture at or above its mutual deliquescence point, handed to mesa_ptc (NOT transcribed here); 4 no salt present, all solid; 5 below the mutual deliquescence point, all solid. Reads the consumer's crh_ok, upper_leg, x_t, salt_code and mdrh.",
          "body": {
            "op": "ifelse",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "and",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "<",
                    "args": [
                      "x",
                      "pp.crh"
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "op": ">",
                    "args": [
                      "crh_ok",
                      0.5
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              1.0,
              {
                "op": "ifelse",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": ">",
                    "args": [
                      "upper_leg",
                      0.5
                    ]
                  },
                  2.0,
                  {
                    "op": "ifelse",
                    "args": [
                      {
                        "op": "and",
                        "args": [
                          {
                            "op": "<",
                            "args": [
                              "x_t",
                              1.0
                            ]
                          },
                          {
                            "op": ">",
                            "args": [
                              "x_t",
                              0.0
                            ]
                          }
                        ]
                      },
                      6.0,
                      {
                        "op": "ifelse",
                        "args": [
                          {
                            "op": "==",
                            "args": [
                              "salt_code",
                              0.0
                            ]
                          },
                          4.0,
                          {
                            "op": "ifelse",
                            "args": [
                              {
                                "op": "<",
                                "args": [
                                  {
                                    "op": "*",
                                    "args": [
                                      "x",
                                      100.0
                                    ]
                                  },
                                  "mdrh"
                                ]
                              },
                              5.0,
                              6.0
                            ]
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "wet_volume": {
          "params": [
            "x"
          ],
          "description": "Wet volume vol_dry + 1e-3 W(x) of the fully deliquesced bin at water activity x, cm3 per cm3 of air.",
          "body": {
            "op": "+",
            "args": [
              "vol_dry",
              {
                "op": "*",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "apply_expression_template",
                    "args": [],
                    "name": "zsr_water",
                    "bindings": {
                      "a": "x"
                    }
                  },
                  "pp.water_to_g_per_cm3"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "wet_diameter": {
          "params": [
            "x"
          ],
          "description": "Volume-mean wet diameter (6 V/(N pi))^(1/3) (calculate_kelvin), cm, with pi and 1/3 at their binary32 values.",
          "body": {
            "op": "^",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "/",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "*",
                    "args": [
                      6.0,
                      {
                        "op": "apply_expression_template",
                        "args": [],
                        "name": "wet_volume",
                        "bindings": {
                          "x": "x"
                        }
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "op": "*",
                    "args": [
                      "num",
                      "pp.pi_k"
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              "pp.third"
            ]
          }
        },
        "solution_tension": {
          "params": [
            "x"
          ],
          "description": "Solution surface tension sigma_water + 49 (1 - x) (calculate_kelvin), with the B28 unit slip in sigma_water.",
          "body": {
            "op": "+",
            "args": [
              "sigma_water",
              {
                "op": "*",
                "args": [
                  49.0,
                  {
                    "op": "-",
                    "args": [
                      1.0,
                      "x"
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "kelvin_series": {
          "params": [
            "t"
          ],
          "description": "MOSAIC's third-order expansion of exp(t): 1 + t (1 + t/2 (1 + t/3)).",
          "body": {
            "op": "+",
            "args": [
              1.0,
              {
                "op": "*",
                "args": [
                  "t",
                  {
                    "op": "+",
                    "args": [
                      1.0,
                      {
                        "op": "*",
                        "args": [
                          0.5,
                          "t",
                          {
                            "op": "+",
                            "args": [
                              1.0,
                              {
                                "op": "/",
                                "args": [
                                  "t",
                                  3.0
                                ]
                              }
                            ]
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "kelvin_factor": {
          "params": [
            "x"
          ],
          "description": "Kelvin factor of the fully deliquesced bin at water activity x: the series of 72 sigma/(R T Dp), R = 8.3144e7 erg/(mol K).",
          "body": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "kelvin_series",
            "bindings": {
              "t": {
                "op": "/",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "*",
                    "args": [
                      72.0,
                      {
                        "op": "apply_expression_template",
                        "args": [],
                        "name": "solution_tension",
                        "bindings": {
                          "x": "x"
                        }
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "op": "*",
                    "args": [
                      "pp.r_cgs",
                      "t_k",
                      {
                        "op": "apply_expression_template",
                        "args": [],
                        "name": "wet_diameter",
                        "bindings": {
                          "x": "x"
                        }
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "kelvin_update": {
          "params": [
            "x"
          ],
          "description": "One pass of aerosol_phase_state's loop from iterate x: where MESA leaves the bin liquid and the relative change |(x' - x)/x| of x' = rh_pc*0.01/K(x) exceeds the tolerance, x'; otherwise x (the loop has exited, so the sequence holds).",
          "body": {
            "op": "ifelse",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "and",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "==",
                    "args": [
                      {
                        "op": "apply_expression_template",
                        "args": [],
                        "name": "mesa_path",
                        "bindings": {
                          "x": "x"
                        }
                      },
                      2.0
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "op": ">",
                    "args": [
                      {
                        "op": "abs",
                        "args": [
                          {
                            "op": "/",
                            "args": [
                              {
                                "op": "-",
                                "args": [
                                  {
                                    "op": "/",
                                    "args": [
                                      "aw0",
                                      {
                                        "op": "apply_expression_template",
                                        "args": [],
                                        "name": "kelvin_factor",
                                        "bindings": {
                                          "x": "x"
                                        }
                                      }
                                    ]
                                  },
                                  "x"
                                ]
                              },
                              "x"
                            ]
                          }
                        ]
                      },
                      "kelvin_tol"
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "op": "/",
                "args": [
                  "aw0",
                  {
                    "op": "apply_expression_template",
                    "args": [],
                    "name": "kelvin_factor",
                    "bindings": {
                      "x": "x"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              "x"
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      "variables": {
        "rh_pc": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "percent",
          "default": 60.0,
          "description": "Relative humidity in percent, rh_pc = 100.*relhumclm(k), formed by mosaic() in default REAL and held in real(kind=8); every water activity below starts from rh_pc*0.01."
        },
        "t_k": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "K",
          "default": 290.0,
          "description": "Air temperature t_k."
        },
        "num": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1/cm^3",
          "default": 1000.0,
          "description": "Bin number concentration num_a(ibin), particles per cm3 of air."
        },
        "aer_t": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "nmol/m^3",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Total species amounts aer(ja, jtotal, ibin) after conform_electrolytes, nmol per m3 of air.",
          "shape": [
            "aer"
          ]
        },
        "elec": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "nmol/m^3",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Total electrolyte amounts electrolyte(je, jtotal, ibin) as conform_electrolytes left them, nmol per m3 of air.",
          "shape": [
            "el"
          ]
        },
        "water_hyst": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "kg/m^3",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "water_a_hyst(ibin): the water the bin carried on the upper hysteresis leg at the end of the previous MOSAIC step (mosaic_dynamic_solver), or 0 on the lower leg."
        },
        "aer_h": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "nmol/m^3",
          "description": "The H+ implied by charge balance of the totals, (2 SO4 + NO3 + Cl + MSA + 2 CO3) - (2 Ca + Na + NH4); the Fortran adds this nmol amount straight into the ng and ncc sums, i.e. at an implied 1 g/mol and 1 g/cm3."
        },
        "mass_dry": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "g/cm^3",
          "description": "Dry mass of the bin mass_dry_a, g per cm3 of air."
        },
        "vol_dry": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Dry volume of the bin vol_dry_a, cm3 of particle per cm3 of air."
        },
        "v_kappa": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "nmol*cm^3/(mol*m^3)",
          "description": "kappa-weighted dry volume of the non-electrolytes, read by the zsr_water template (as in aerosol_water_zsr.esm)."
        },
        "water_up": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/m^3",
          "description": "aerosol_water_up: the ZSR water of the TOTAL electrolytes at a fixed water activity 0.6 (binary32), no kappa term and no fit-range clamp (bin_molality_60), each term scaled by 1e-9 before summing."
        },
        "upper_leg": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "1 where water_a_hyst > 0.5 water_a_up (mhyst_method = uporlo_waterhyst): MESA forces the bin onto the upper (fully deliquesced) branch."
        },
        "x_t": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "calculate_xt on the totals: (NH4 + Na + 2 Ca)/(SO4 + MSA/2), or -1 without sulfate or MSA."
        },
        "elec_sum": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "nmol/m^3",
          "description": "Sum of the total electrolytes, or 1 where it is zero (MESA's guard)."
        },
        "epercent": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "percent",
          "description": "Mole percent of each electrolyte in the total, 100 E_e / sum E.",
          "shape": [
            "el"
          ]
        },
        "crh_ok": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "1 where the composition allows efflorescence at the crystallization point: X_T > 1 or X_T < 0, and neither Ca(NO3)2 nor CaCl2 above ptol_mol_astem percent."
        },
        "salt_code": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "MESA's salt-combination code: the sum of jsalt_index over the salts present above ptol_mol_astem percent (0: none)."
        },
        "mdrh_index": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Index of the salt combination's mutual deliquescence curve: jsulf_poor(code) where X_T >= 2 or X_T < 0, else jsulf_rich(code); 0 where no salt is present."
        },
        "mdrh": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "percent",
          "description": "Mutual deliquescence relative humidity of the combination (drh_mutual): 10 for the Ca(NO3)2/CaCl2 mixtures (indices 7, 8, 34-51), else the cubic d_1 + T(d_2 + T(d_3 + T d_4)) + 1."
        },
        "sigma_water": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "dyn/cm",
          "description": "Surface tension of pure water as update_thermodynamic_constants forms it, 0.2358 tau^1.256 (1 - 0.625 tau), tau = (647.15 - T)/647.15. THE FORMULA GIVES N/m (about 0.072) and calculate_kelvin adds it to a term in dyn/cm (FORTRAN_BUGS B28); reproduced as written, so this is 1000 times too small for the dyn/cm it is used as."
        },
        "kelvin_tol": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Relative tolerance of the Kelvin iteration: binary32 1e-2 where rh_pc <= 99, else 1e-6."
        },
        "aw0": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "The ambient water activity ah2o = rh_pc*0.01 (binary32 0.01), the first iterate."
        },
        "aw_it": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "The bin water activity ah2o_a at each pass of the Kelvin loop: aw_it[1] = aw0, aw_it[i] = kelvin_update(aw_it[i-1]). A causal recurrence over the iteration axis (esm 4.3.1.1), justified below.",
          "shape": [
            "it"
          ]
        },
        "ah2o_a": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "The bin water activity ah2o_a(ibin) aerosol_phase_state leaves: the last iterate."
        },
        "niter": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Number of passes of the loop (iter_kelvin): one plus the number of iterates that moved."
        },
        "path": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "The MESA branch at the final water activity (see mesa_path). 6 means mesa_ptc decided the phase, which this component does not transcribe: none of its other outputs is meaningful there."
        },
        "liquid": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "1 where the bin ends fully liquid (path 2)."
        },
        "state": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "jaerosolstate: 2 all liquid (path 2), 1 all solid (paths 1, 4, 5), 0 where mesa_ptc decides (path 6, not transcribed)."
        },
        "jhyst": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "jhyst_leg on exit: 1 (upper) when liquid, 0 (lower) when solid."
        },
        "water": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/m^3",
          "description": "Liquid water water_a: the ZSR water of the total electrolytes at the final water activity when liquid, 0 when solid."
        },
        "mass_wet": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "g/cm^3",
          "description": "Wet mass mass_dry + 1e-3 water (meaningful when liquid; on a solid exit the Fortran leaves the previous pass's value)."
        },
        "vol_wet": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Wet volume vol_dry + 1e-3 water (as mass_wet)."
        },
        "dpmv": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "cm",
          "description": "Volume-mean wet diameter of the liquid bin at the final water activity."
        },
